WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.525
As each population becomes
cloud-mastered, retarget its provisioning.

2
00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:09.321
Once its sync cycle completes, move
it out of the HR-to-AD scope and

3
00:00:09.321 --> 00:00:14.750
into the HR-to-Entra configuration,
leaving the AD leg dormant but intact.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:20.838
Microsoft lists entry checks: HR writes
Entra ID directly, no on-premises Exchange,

5
00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:25.762
no federation for those users, and
no apps that bind with passwords.

6
00:00:25.762 --> 00:00:27.775
Make those your per-population gate.

7
00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:33.434
One honest caveat: whether this
source-of-authority transfer works in GCC is still

8
00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:37.012
unverified, so give that
question an owner and a date,

9
00:00:37.012 --> 00:00:39.925
and plan on the AD-mastered
path by default.

10
00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:43.713
On the right is what still needs
AD, each with its response.

11
00:00:43.713 --> 00:00:47.180
And if a cutover goes wrong,
pause the provisioning job,

12
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.180
which keeps its state, quarantine the
batch, and fall back to the prior process.
